{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790727010,"nonce":"5zzZejWISdiUd3SxFl2XIvGbwLw=","message":"Lock audit: ZyntaxLlvmBackend::compile and resume_points both hold its inner Mutex across the complete LLVM operation: HIR-to-LLVM lowering, optimization, MCJIT engine creation/codegen, helper publication, and pointer lookup. More Beadie promotion workers cannot overlap LLVM work with this shape. The main execution thread does not acquire this mutex, so it does not directly stop interpreted/Cranelift execution, but LLVM promotions and late resume-point builds serialize behind it. Batching functions, or giving each broker job an independent LLVM backend/context whose engines are retained by an Arc-owned pool, must remove or shard this mutex as part of this issue.","files":null}]}